# Without this, `COPY . .` drags the HOST's node_modules into the image and
# overwrites the Linux dependency tree installed inside it — pnpm's symlink
# farm and any native binary become wrong for the container's platform, and
# the build fails with a confusing "cannot find module" on a package that is
# obviously installed.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — regenerated inside the image.
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
out
**/out
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local state and secrets. `.env.example` is intentionally NOT ignored.
#
# The `**/` prefix is NOT decoration. A bare `.env` pattern matches ONLY at the
# build-context root — `apps/web/.env.local` sails straight past it and into the
# image, where Next.js then auto-loads it at runtime. That exact bug shipped a
# live bot token inside a locally built image and silently overrode the
# container's rate-limit config. Every secret pattern below must be `**/`-rooted,
# and ci.yml asserts the result by scanning the built image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.dev.vars
.wrangler
**/.wrangler

# Test artefacts
coverage
**/coverage
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
test-results
**/test-results

# VCS and editor noise
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Docs do not affect the build.
*.md
docs
